  "description": "Certificate of Lawful Development (Proposed): Provision of two shipping containers at the end of the tennis courts for storage of sports equipment, grounds maintenance equipment; ground levelling preparation or base for the storage containers",
  "development_type": "Certificates of Lawful Development",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal is therefore NOT a lawful development.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development would not be located within the curtilage of the existing school which would fail to comply with the parameters of permitted development as set out under M.2(a) from Schedule 2, Part 7, Class M of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development has not demonstrated that the development would not exceed 25% of the cumulative footprint of the school and would therefore not comply with the parameters of permitted development as set out under M.1(a)(i) and (ii) from Schedule 2, Part 7, Class M of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal would result in a development which would result in the loss of land used as a playing field at any time in the 5 years before the development commenced and remaining in this use could no longer be so used. The proposal would therefore not comply within the parameters of permitted development as set out under M.1(c) from Schedule 2, Part 7, Class M of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development has not demonstrated that the predominant use of the existing buildings on the premises is for the provision of education and would therefore not comply within the parameters of permitted development as set out under M.1(g)(i) from Schedule 2, Part 7, Class M of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
